WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.680
46 new projects in 16 EU states are meant to cut reliance on any one mineral supplier. This is Omni View Europe, Episode 20. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. The European Commission said today it chose that set from 102 applications. By 2030, the Critical Raw Materials Act wants EU capacity to cover at least a tenth of yearly use in extraction, two fifths in processing, and a quarter in recycling. Eight dig the ore, 11 process it, and 19 recycle it.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.960
8 more combined stages, 3 mine and process, 5 process and recycle.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.080
Together they touch 15 of the 17 strategic materials in the act.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:46.340
Batteries take the biggest share, 7 lithium, 12 nickel, 10 cobalt, 5 manganese, 4 graphite,

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:52.280
2 magnesium projects and 3 tungsten projects sit with defense and aerospace, 4 rare earth

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.840
projects feed permanent magnets.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.940
The commission says this round on top of 47 EU projects picked in March last year and 13

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.420
outside the EU picked in June last year should move those targets.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:06.500
Business review says two of the new ones are in Romania.

