00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.980
In the wider world, Europe's goods gap with China hit

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:22.080
359.3 billion euros last year, more than twice the 2019 figure.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.060
Think China says Brussels will not accept a deficit,

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.360
it puts at 1.1 billion euros a day,

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.600
and blames unfair Chinese practices.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.980
Beijing says the numbers do not hold.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:37.500
Nearly half the trade is intermediate goods European firms buy, upgrade and sell-on, so

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.960
China books the surplus and Europe takes the profit.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.500
Beijing also points to a long EU surplus in services.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:48.300
Trade Commissioner Maro Sefkovich spent two days in Beijing with Commerce Minister Wang

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:53.300
Wentao from October 8th before an EU summit in Brussels this week on Chinese competition.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:59.400
The talks ended late Friday, October 9th, on a 16-point consensus covering trade, investment,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.960
export controls and intellectual property.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:05.220
China agreed to limit hybrid vehicle exports to the block

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.900
to head off harsher curbs.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.320
Think China says that is unlikely to reset the relationship soon

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.680
and that it only buys time for more talks in January and March.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:17.160
The case on both sides in France is what to do with public debt

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.540
the state already holds itself.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.620
Immanuel Mulan, governor of the central bank,

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:24.280
wants large budget cuts so rising interest rates

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:25.800
do not slowly choke the country.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:30.500
Jean-Luc Mélenchon, leader of LaFrance and Sumis and a presidential contender,

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:35.740
wants a different treatment of about 600 billion euros, 673 billion dollars,

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:38.460
18% of France's aggregate public debt.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:42.360
Those are government bonds the central bank owns and will keep until they mature.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:47.140
The essay says that at maturity taxpayers would pay more tax, or borrow again,

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.060
to repay their own central bank.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:53.940
Mélenchon's case is that one arm of the French state should not borrow 600 billion euros

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:58.300
just to pay another arm. He wants a swap between the Treasury and the Central Bank that,

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:03.740
in practice, retires that debt and frees money for investment. The essay says the idea comes

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:09.200
from debt swap proposals, a then-Greek finance minister made in 2015. Mulan's side treats

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:14.000
spending cuts as the way to keep interest costs from closing in. Melanchand's side treats the

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:19.440
internal debt as a loop that cuts would not break. A sign of progress, Nordic Mining's third quarter

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.140
